# Network shares, for `sys net`.
#
#   name | url | what it is
#
# The url must include the share name, or Finder stops to ask which one you
# want.
#
# The password comes from the login Keychain, where Finder saved it the first
# time you connected and ticked "Remember this password". Nothing here stores
# or types a password: those Keychain items are locked to Finder, so `sys net`
# hands it the url and lets Finder authenticate.
#
# Only the dwkns shares are here. The NAS also has an admin account with its
# own shares, but macOS keeps ONE SMB session per server, so mounting as both
# accounts at once needs the same NAS reached by two different names. Not
# worth it: for admin work, ssh in instead.

dwkns-nas    | smb://dwkns@192.168.5.45/dwkns-nas   | your files on the NAS
backup-nas   | smb://dwkns@192.168.5.45/backup-nas  | backups, as dwkns
